    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// create a list of articles instead of having three separate arrays\nconst titles = $input.first().json.title;\nconst links = $input.first().json.link;\nconst snippets = $input.first().json.contentSnippet;\n\nlet articleList = '';\n\nfor (let i = 0; i < titles.length; i++) {\n  const snippet = snippets[i] && snippets[i].trim() !== '' \n    ? snippets[i] \n    : '(no summary available, use title only)';\n  \n  articleList += `${i + 1}. Title: ${titles[i]}\\nSnippet: ${snippet}\\nLink: ${links[i]}\\n\\n`;\n}\n\nreturn [{ json: { articleList } }];"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1136, 256],
      "id": "a2eb3ee1-1162-4288-8f1d-6dc4b5c6678d",
      "name": "Code in JavaScript"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-3.5-flash",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-3.5-flash"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are an AI news curator producing a daily Telegram digest.\n\nINPUT: A list of AI-related articles from the last 24 hours, each with a title, snippet, and link.\n{{ $json.articleList }}\n\nSTEP 1 — SELECT\nChoose the 5 to 8 most genuinely important stories from the list. Prioritize:\n- Major model releases or version updates from well-known labs\n- Significant research breakthroughs\n- Notable industry shifts (funding, acquisitions, policy, major partnerships)\n- Announcements with wide, immediate impact\n\nExclude:\n- Minor feature tweaks, routine product housekeeping, or maintenance posts\n- Duplicate or near-duplicate coverage of the same story (pick the single best source)\n- Opinion pieces, listicles, or \"roundup\" articles with no new information\n\nIf fewer than 5 stories meet the bar, include only the ones that genuinely qualify — do not pad the list with weak stories to hit a minimum.\n\nSTEP 2 — SUMMARIZE\nFor each selected story, write exactly 1-2 sentences in plain, neutral language a non-expert could understand. No jargon unless it's the subject itself (then briefly explain it).\n\nIf a snippet reads \"(no summary available, use title only)\", base the summary strictly on the title. Do not invent, assume, or infer details not present in the title.\n\nSTEP 3 — FORMAT\nOutput ONLY the digest below, using Telegram Markdown. No preamble, no closing remarks, no explanation of your choices, no notes about excluded stories.\n\n🤖 *AI News Digest — {{ $today.format('DDD') }}*\n\n1. *[Title]*\n[1-2 sentence summary]\n🔗 [Link]\n\n2. *[Title]*\n[1-2 sentence summary]\n🔗 [Link]\n\n(continue numbering sequentially for all selected stories)\n\nRULES:\n- Titles must match the source exactly (no rewriting for style).\n- Never fabricate a link — only use links provided in the input.\n- Never exceed 2 sentences per summary.\n- If the input list is empty or contains no qualifying stories, output only: \"No major AI news today.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
